  "id": "perceived-reality",
  "term": "perceived reality",
  "definition": "Perceived reality is a person’s experienced version of what is real, shaped by the information sources they use and how they interpret that information. In this study context, this subjective reality appeared more strongly related to depression than some objective or directly measurable conditions.",
